🔹 Program 9: Base Pointer With a Virtual Function

📌 Description

This program demonstrates run-time polymorphism using a virtual function and a base-class pointer.

The base pointer can point to different derived objects. Because "sound()" is declared "virtual", the appropriate derived-class implementation is selected during program execution.

🎯 Concept Used

Run-Time Polymorphism — Virtual Function

💡 Key Point

A base pointer can refer to different derived objects, and a virtual function enables dynamic binding.
